AC3 gap: NStoreCard has ZERO golden test coverage (no golden file exists for
ANY NStoreCard state, including the two new NEARS-3633 variants: closed-
consolidation and popularItems).

Evidence (read-only static check, run against worktree
/Users/Apple/Projects/nears-NEARS-3633-card-convergence, commit ce7827934):

$ find packages/nears_dls/test/golden -type f -name "*.dart"
  ... (29 files listed, e.g. n_item_card_golden_test.dart, n_badge_golden_test.dart, ...)
  -- no n_store_card_golden_test.dart present --

$ grep -rn "matchesGoldenFile\|goldenFileComparator" packages/nears_dls/test/components/n_store_card_test.dart
  -- 0 matches --

By contrast, NItemCard(compact) DOES have full golden coverage:
packages/nears_dls/test/golden/n_item_card_golden_test.dart lines 295-342+,
fileName 'n_item_card_compact', EN+AR x 1.0x+1.3x variants, backed by
packages/nears_dls/test/golden/goldens/ci/n_item_card_compact.png.

NStoreCard's closed-consolidation and popularItems variants ARE covered by
widget/behavioral tests (packages/nears_dls/test/components/n_store_card_test.dart,
groups "NEARS-3633 closed-state consolidation" and "NEARS-3633 popularItems
(thumbnail strip)", all passing), and by catalog.yaml entries and storybook
use-cases (widgetbook/lib/components/n_store_card_stories.dart). Only the
GOLDEN (pixel-regression) layer is missing, which is one of the three things
AC3 explicitly requires ("Catalog entry + storybook use-case + golden exist
for every new variant/slot").
